# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Paths excluded from `git archive` (and therefore from the starter/clone zip
# produced by `pnpm export:starter` / `pnpm export:clone`). Dev-only, not part
# of the runnable application a fresh-install user needs. NOTE: docs/ is
# intentionally NOT excluded — the operational runbooks ship with the bundle.
apps/e2e/         export-ignore
loadtest/         export-ignore
.claude/          export-ignore
.github/          export-ignore
.vscode/          export-ignore
CLAUDE.md         export-ignore
*.test.ts         export-ignore

# Decode's real publisher content (posts / pages / media) — kept in the repo
# for `export:clone` and dev seeding, but stripped from the BLANK
# `export:starter` so a fresh publisher gets a clean CMS with no Decode data.
# `export:clone` restores the live DB dump (not these fixtures), so it is
# unaffected. NOTE: this only strips the DATA; the CMS theme CODE
# (apps/web/themes/{default,basic}) ships on purpose — both are part of the CMS
# and receive updates. Only a publisher's CUSTOM theme is excluded, below.

# PING's CUSTOM theme — the publisher's own hand-built work, not part of the
# CMS. `pnpm export:starter` ships only the two CMS themes (default + basic);
# a custom theme belongs to the install that made it and is never distributed,
# never updated by the CMS, and would otherwise hand a new publisher another
# publisher's design, brand marks and content.
# See docs/phase-3-versioning-and-updates-plan.md.
apps/web/themes/ping/            export-ignore
packages/blocks/src/themes/ping/ export-ignore
apps/api/fixtures/ping/          export-ignore
